From 8acd97b72128cd3b4eff5ca8a5d784e39de66cde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:05:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 75/94] ASoC: codecs: hiby-hm100: log an unreachable PCM rate
 at debug level

q6asm-dai now offers PCM on MultiMedia1 only at the rates the FPGA has
a PCM rate word for, as it offers DSD only at the DSD rates, so the
PCM half of the hw_params rate check is no more reachable than the DSD
half. Log it at debug level like that one, and say why in the comment,
which still had the FE taking 8 to 32 kHz.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
 sound/soc/codecs/hiby-hm100.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/hiby-hm100.c b/sound/soc/codecs/hiby-hm100.c
index 8fd2311a9..992363337 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/hiby-hm100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/hiby-hm100.c
@@ -1322,15 +1322,16 @@ static int hm100_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, struct snd_pcm_h
 	if (substream->stream != SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK)
 		return 0;
 	/*
-	 * A DSD stream needs a DSD rate word (mode 2): DSD64..512. q6asm-dai's hw rule offers
-	 * DSD only at those FE rates, so the DSD case is not reached from MultiMedia1; PCM
-	 * still is (the FE takes 8000..32000, the BE fixup hides rate_min).
+	 * A DSD stream needs a DSD rate word (mode 2): DSD64..512, a PCM stream one of the
+	 * others. q6asm-dai's hw rules offer DSD only at those FE rates and PCM only at these
+	 * (the BE fixup hides rate_min from the FE), so neither case is reached from
+	 * MultiMedia1.
 	 */
 	if (w < 0 || !!dsd != ((w & 3) == 2)) {
 		if (dsd)
 			dev_dbg(h->dev, "DSD rate %u not supported\n", dsd);
 		else
-			dev_err(h->dev, "PCM rate %u not supported\n", rate);
+			dev_dbg(h->dev, "PCM rate %u not supported\n", rate);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
